# One key under each modifier in turn.
#
# The text is what macOS hands over, which is why ⌃A carries none: the
# platform gives a control character there, and the encoder derives that from
# the key rather than being told it twice. ⌥A arrives as the character Option
# already made, with the modifier marked as spent on it.
#
# The release encodes nothing, which is the point of that line, and it sits
# between two keys that do encode something so its silence is held in place
# by what is on either side of it.
#
# ⌘ is not here. What a command key comes to is the platform's answer rather
# than the terminal's — macOS sends no text under one because it is the app's
# to act on, Linux sends the character — and a golden two CI runners read the
# same way cannot hold both. The half knotty runs on is pinned in
# knotty-ffi's `a_command_key_sends_the_child_nothing` instead.

# A prompt to type at, so the screen the golden holds is one a terminal
# would really be showing when the keys below arrive.
out "$ "

key A "a"
key A ctrl
key A shift "A"
key A release "a"
key A alt consumed=alt "å"
